# Repository Pattern

Repositories handle data access and mapping between Prisma models and domain entities.

## File Structure

```
repositories/{entity-name}/
├── {operation}.ts         # Individual operations (create.ts, get-all.ts, etc.)
├── index.ts               # Repository aggregator
└── mappers/
    └── {entity}.mapper.ts # Prisma model ↔ Entity mapper
```

## Repository Implementation Pattern

### Individual Operation File (`{operation}.ts`)

```typescript
import type { PrismaClient } from '@prisma/client';
import type { Entity } from '@/entities/{entity}/{entity}.js';
import { toEntity } from './mappers/{entity}.mapper.js';

// Define input data interface
export interface OperationEntityData {
  // Properties needed for this operation
  field: string;
}

// Repository factory function
export const initOperationEntityRepository = (prisma: PrismaClient) => {
  return async (data: OperationEntityData): Promise<Entity> => {
    // 1. Perform database operation
    const model = await prisma.{entity}.{operation}({
      data: {
        field: data.field,
      },
    });

    // 2. Map to domain entity
    return toEntity(model);
  };
};
```

**Key Points:**
- Export a factory function named `init{Operation}{Entity}Repository`
- Takes `PrismaClient` as parameter (dependency injection)
- Returns an async function that performs the operation
- Define input interface for type safety
- Always map Prisma models to domain entities using mappers
- NO business logic—only data access

### Repository Aggregator (`index.ts`)

```typescript
import type { PrismaClient } from '@prisma/client';
import { initCreateEntityRepository } from './create.js';
import { initGetAllEntitiesRepository } from './get-all.js';
import { initGetEntityByIdRepository } from './get-by-id.js';
import { initUpdateEntityRepository } from './update.js';
import { initDeleteEntityRepository } from './delete.js';

export const initEntityRepositories = (prisma: PrismaClient) => {
  return {
    create: initCreateEntityRepository(prisma),
    getAll: initGetAllEntitiesRepository(prisma),
    getById: initGetEntityByIdRepository(prisma),
    update: initUpdateEntityRepository(prisma),
    delete: initDeleteEntityRepository(prisma),
  };
};

export type EntityRepositories = ReturnType<typeof initEntityRepositories>;
```

**Key Points:**
- Export `init{Entity}Repositories` function
- Return object with all operations as properties
- Export type using `ReturnType<typeof ...>`
- Use consistent naming: `getAll`, `getById`, `create`, `update`, `delete`

### Repository Mapper (`mappers/{entity}.mapper.ts`)

```typescript
import type { Entity } from '@/entities/{entity}/{entity}.js';
import type { Model } from '@prisma/client';

// Database Model → Domain Entity
export const toEntity = (model: Model): Entity => {
  return {
    id: model.id,
    field: model.field,
    createdAt: model.createdAt,
    updatedAt: model.updatedAt,
  };
};

// Domain Entity → Database Model (for updates, if needed)
export const toModel = (entity: Partial<Entity>): Partial<Model> => {
  return {
    field: entity.field,
    // Don't include id, createdAt if not updating them
  };
};
```

**Key Points:**
- Export `toEntity` for model → entity conversion (always needed)
- Export `toModel` for entity → model conversion (if needed for updates)
- Handle type conversions (Date objects remain as Date in both)
- Keep pure mapping logic—no business rules

## Common Patterns

### Get All
```typescript
export const initGetAllEntitiesRepository = (prisma: PrismaClient) => {
  return async (): Promise<Entity[]> => {
    const models = await prisma.entity.findMany({
      orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' },
    });
    return models.map(toEntity);
  };
};
```

### Get By ID
```typescript
export const initGetEntityByIdRepository = (prisma: PrismaClient) => {
  return async (id: string): Promise<Entity | null> => {
    const model = await prisma.entity.findUnique({
      where: { id },
    });
    return model ? toEntity(model) : null;
  };
};
```

### Create
```typescript
export interface CreateEntityData {
  field: string;
}

export const initCreateEntityRepository = (prisma: PrismaClient) => {
  return async (data: CreateEntityData): Promise<Entity> => {
    const model = await prisma.entity.create({
      data: {
        field: data.field,
      },
    });
    return toEntity(model);
  };
};
```

### Update
```typescript
export interface UpdateEntityData {
  id: string;
  field?: string;
}

export const initUpdateEntityRepository = (prisma: PrismaClient) => {
  return async (data: UpdateEntityData): Promise<Entity> => {
    const { id, ...updateData } = data;
    const model = await prisma.entity.update({
      where: { id },
      data: updateData,
    });
    return toEntity(model);
  };
};
```

### Delete
```typescript
export const initDeleteEntityRepository = (prisma: PrismaClient) => {
  return async (id: string): Promise<void> => {
    await prisma.entity.delete({
      where: { id },
    });
  };
};
```

## Checklist for New Repository

- [ ] Create `repositories/{entity-name}/` directory
- [ ] Create operation files: `create.ts`, `get-all.ts`, `get-by-id.ts`, `update.ts`, `delete.ts`
- [ ] Create `mappers/{entity-name}.mapper.ts` with `toEntity` function
- [ ] Create `index.ts` aggregator
- [ ] Add to `repositories/index.ts` root aggregator
- [ ] Use factory pattern: `init{Operation}{Entity}Repository`
- [ ] Always map Prisma models to domain entities
- [ ] Export proper TypeScript types
